@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-mergeability-is-separate-from-checks
A pull request GitHub marks conflicting or dirty MUST show its merge conflicts on the
Overview even when its checks pass; passing checks MUST NOT imply that it is ready to
merge. Missing, unknown or unrecognized mergeability MUST remain checking, and an
overview kept from a prior opening or belonging to an older observed head MUST NOT
enable merging until a matching fresh overview arrives. Conflicts MUST override a
contradictory cached ready verdict (Tavi, 20 Oct 2026, "a PR would have merge conflicts ...
yet Pully would show it as being all good").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-overview-preserves-wire-and-permissions
Android and iOS MUST use one parser for the existing overview wire response, including
viewer permissions, lifecycle, checks, commits and timeline. The parser MUST preserve
the existing ownership requirement for editing title/description and the current-head,
fresh-response requirement for a ready merge verdict. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS decision; DESIGN.md rules 83 and 110 and the 20 Oct mergeability and
merged-lifecycle decisions.
@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-overview-opening-and-lists-retain-policy
The shared opening models MUST retain list-known lifecycle and title facts before
the overview arrives. A recorded merge MUST outrank a later open cache, and newer
known open facts MAY replace closed facts after reopening. File sections MUST retain
their whole-label fold keys, say a shared prefix once and never cut its run at Show
more. Only positive PR number labels with repository coordinates MAY produce a
canonical GitHub PR URL. Source: existing pr-opens-at-once, pr-lifecycle-is-visible,
pr-groups-say-a-shared-start-once and pr-number-opens-github, shared by Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-overview-html-is-inert-and-bounded-to-text
GitHub body HTML MUST remain converted to inert Markdown by the existing converter;
it MUST NOT execute scripts or create a WebView. Numeric entities MUST preserve
valid supplementary characters, and malformed or out-of-range values MUST remain
literal text rather than throw while the remote description or comment is read.
Source: existing PrHtml behavior, DESIGN.md rule 53 and the accepted 21 Oct 2026
shared Overview reading extraction.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-diff-model-preserves-existing-policy
Both hosts MUST use the existing diff expansion, split pairing, selected-code,
annotation-anchor, noisy-file and word-emphasis policies. File trees MUST preserve
English locale ordering, single-child folder compression and all/some/none review
state. A one-sided file MUST remain unified even when split is selected. Source:
existing DiffModel and FileTree behavior, DESIGN.md rules 93 and 94, H10, and Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-diff-emphasis-belongs-to-row-object
Word-emphasis ranges MUST belong to the exact diff-line object they were computed
for. Distinct rows whose data compare equal MUST NOT overwrite each other's
ranges or receive a different row's emphasis. Source: the existing lineEmphasis
IdentityHashMap policy retained by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared diff/code plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] shared-tour-progress-retains-reading-policy
The Tour progress ring MUST follow the existing reading-line interpolation and finish
at the page end, including a short last stop. A missing or empty stop list MUST remain
at zero. Source: existing tour-strip-is-calm, DESIGN.md rule 97, preserved by Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision.
